      "patch": "@@ -50,3 +50,7 @@ Purpose: give AI a small, trustworthy map without destroying or blindly copying\n - When a curator edits symbols.tsv in a dedicated worktree, invoke that worktree's tools/v9_coverage.py with `--root <research-root> --out <isolated-kb> --symbols <isolated-kb>/symbols.tsv --export`. This keeps the indexed original PE/V9 and research.sqlite under the authorized read-only research root while using the curated symbol dictionary from the isolated worktree.\n - Without --symbols, the backward-compatible default reads <research-root>/knowledge/symbols.tsv, which may be an unrelated user checkout. Never equate that older dictionary with the isolated candidate version.\n - The full V9 function crosswalk remains in the local research root's knowledge/generated directory; GitHub receives only lightweight report and priority TSVs. Candidate counts are descriptive STATIC metadata, not proof or READY.\n+\n+## User directive 2026-11-01: publish reusable research, not just local notes\n+The latest user-approved rule is [RESEARCH_INTAKE_PROTOCOL_20261101.md](RESEARCH_INTAKE_PROTOCOL_20261101.md).\n+The earlier prohibition on A-E/REA editing the **curated KB** (`symbols.tsv`, `structs.tsv`, `REF_*`, `develop`) remains. An explicit exception now allows each source owner to archive **their own sanitized, source-linked, potentially VERIFY** research in a PRIVATE `research/intake/<owner>/` path on an isolated owner branch. The dedicated curator alone accepts into `develop` by non-force fast-forward after audit and preserves source confidence, corrections and safety refusals. Research capture must end in one of PUBLISHED_INTAKE / CURATED / DUPLICATE_LINKED / BLOCKED / OFFLINE_UNSYNCED with a specific next action; creating only a local report does not complete the GitHub discoverability obligation.",
      "raw_url": "https://github.com/ButaMonky/Hakushin067-Research-Knowledge/raw/f48ee7c0fd8ef9520dc959c2786c8273ce1815cb/KNOWLEDGE_CURATION_PROTOCOL.md",
